> Conclusion and references

Actual projected extents explain each candidate and the original area savings.
The orientation theorem justifies the candidate set, while explicit
implementation counts establish the quadratic hull scan. Floating projections,
representability guards and strict comparison rules remain part of the result's
practical limits.

[Freeman and Shapira, Determining the minimum-area encasing rectangle for an arbitrary closed curve (1975)|https://doi.org/10.1145/360881.360919]
gives the hull-edge orientation result. This implementation scans orientations
directly rather than maintaining moving calipers.

> Verification

The ten-report batch passes95 CTest cases,31 directly instrumented ASan/UBSan
cases,83 compiled and executed public examples,363/363 scoped documentation
definitions and ten representative hovers. Independent Python integer
arithmetic, MT19937-64/variation replay, graph sets, analytic interpolation,
circle boundary enumeration and actual-sample integration reconstruction agree
on915459 captured records. All six original RMS summaries are separately checked
using96 native MISER estimates and1600000 independently reproduced
plain-comparator points. Frozen valid-input comparisons include the original
seeded solver paths and full MOEA/D fronts. Ten checkout headers and ten
identically installed development headers compile independently, and an
installed-header native consumer links and runs. Each report has four executed
complete programs, four reviewed native figures and both HTML/Markdown exports
with computed-result and image-byte checks. This is a scoped native API audit,
not an installation claim for every language binding. Receipts:
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-234-243/`.
